    },
    {
      "id": "section:0/block:1/seg:0",
      "source": "Key structures and the I/O submission path",
      "source_hash": 18320069661519306025,
      "context_hash": 15802825314737384333,
      "translation": "핵심 구조체와 I/O 제출 경로",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T21:50:07.921334Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:1/block:0/seg:0",
      "source": "Key data structures",
      "source_hash": 886646788032546680,
      "context_hash": 14241229298438585837,
      "translation": "주요 자료 구조",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "Key Data Structures": "주요 자료 구조",
        "data structures": "자료 구조"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T23:28:59.514996Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:1/block:1/seg:0",
      "source": "The block layer uses three key structures:",
      "source_hash": 5064921624696310587,
      "context_hash": 7736538743647941846,
      "translation": "블록 계층은 세 가지 핵심 구조체를 사용합니다:",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "block layer": "블록 계층"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T21:50:07.921334Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:1/block:3/seg:0",
      "source": "struct gendisk",
      "source_hash": 2930529794919193286,
      "context_hash": 6769425159074009905,
      "translation": "struct gendisk",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T21:50:07.921335Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:1/block:4/seg:0",
      "source": "`gendisk` represents a physical disk or virtual block device:",
      "source_hash": 322963402324542942,
      "context_hash": 14442642205060173591,
      "translation": "`gendisk`는 물리 디스크 또는 가상 블록 디바이스를 나타냅니다:",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "block device": "블록 디바이스"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T21:50:07.921335Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:1/block:6/seg:0",
      "source": "struct block_device",
      "source_hash": 11111623415057861214,
      "context_hash": 8633758819412222715,
      "translation": "struct block_device",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T21:50:07.921335Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:1/block:7/seg:0",
      "source": "One `block_device` per partition (or whole disk).",
      "source_hash": 6858578535595972138,
      "context_hash": 7703791033371195689,
      "translation": "파티션(또는 디스크 전체)마다 `block_device` 하나가 있습니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T21:50:07.921335Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:1/block:7/seg:1",
      "source": "This is what filesystems use:",
      "source_hash": 328401227342775726,
      "context_hash": 11479332076834182369,
      "translation": "파일시스템이 사용하는 것이 바로 이 구조체입니다:",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T21:50:07.921335Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:1/block:9/seg:0",
      "source": "struct request_queue",
      "source_hash": 12503021463489420537,
      "context_hash": 1139218893552196304,
      "translation": "struct request_queue",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T21:50:07.921335Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:1/block:10/seg:0",
      "source": "The `request_queue` is the central object for I/O management:",
      "source_hash": 3917353891567953066,
      "context_hash": 8171414506973525299,
      "translation": "`request_queue`는 I/O 관리의 중심 객체입니다:",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T21:50:07.921335Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:2/block:0/seg:0",
      "source": "The submit_bio() path",
      "source_hash": 1026654007904281184,
      "context_hash": 14011558375764980972,
      "translation": "submit_bio() 경로",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T21:50:07.921335Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:3/block:0/seg:0",
      "source": "/proc and /sys for block devices",
      "source_hash": 11403085824807455685,
      "context_hash": 8281040655299747622,
      "translation": "블록 디바이스를 위한 /proc 및 /sys",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "block devices": "블록 디바이스"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T21:50:07.921336Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:4/block:0/seg:0",
      "source": "I/O plug and unplug",
      "source_hash": 15919327735709272923,
      "context_hash": 15884415776586334434,
      "translation": "I/O plug와 unplug",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T21:50:07.921336Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:4/block:1/seg:0",
      "source": "For throughput, the block layer \"plugs\" the queue briefly to accumulate requests before submitting:",
      "source_hash": 8129713480693316899,
      "context_hash": 14068433592959912974,
      "translation": "처리량을 높이기 위해 블록 계층은 요청을 제출하기 전에 큐를 잠시 \"plug\"하여 요청을 모읍니다:",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "block layer": "블록 계층",
        "queue": "큐",
        "throughput": "처리량"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T21:50:07.921336Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:4/block:3/seg:0",
      "source": "This is analogous to TCP's Nagle algorithm: batching small operations into larger ones.",
      "source_hash": 8964198100411587165,
      "context_hash": 5889185367839109731,
      "translation": "이는 작은 작업들을 더 큰 작업으로 묶는다는 점에서 TCP의 Nagle 알고리즘과 유사합니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "TCP": "TCP"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T21:50:07.921336Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:5/block:0/seg:0",
      "source": "I/O schedulers and the NVMe problem",
      "source_hash": 11970706841259449076,
      "context_hash": 15354989675283240176,
      "translation": "I/O 스케줄러와 NVMe 문제",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "NVMe": "NVMe",
        "schedulers": "스케줄러"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T21:50:07.921336Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:5/block:1/seg:0",
      "source": "The `elevator_queue` in `request_queue` is optional.",
      "source_hash": 5822614111071880273,
      "context_hash": 9045280700573591028,
      "translation": "`request_queue`의 `elevator_queue`는 선택 사항입니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T21:50:07.921336Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:5/block:1/seg:1",
      "source": "The I/O scheduler sits between bio submission and hardware dispatch, reordering and merging requests.",
      "source_hash": 12543351606066973627,
      "context_hash": 12406435830920801675,
      "translation": "I/O 스케줄러는 bio 제출과 하드웨어 디스패치 사이에 위치하여 요청을 재정렬하고 병합합니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "hardware": "하드웨어",
        "scheduler": "스케줄러"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T21:50:07.921336Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:5/block:1/seg:2",
      "source": "For HDDs this was essential — an elevator scheduler could turn random writes into sequential I/O, doubling throughput by reducing seek time.",
      "source_hash": 5856693712056571013,
      "context_hash": 13897298281474364408,
      "translation": "HDD에서는 이것이 필수적이었습니다. 엘리베이터 스케줄러는 랜덤 쓰기를 순차 I/O로 바꾸어 탐색 시간(seek time)을 줄임으로써 처리량을 두 배로 늘릴 수 있었습니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "HDDs": "HDD",
        "scheduler": "스케줄러",
        "throughput": "처리량"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T21:50:07.921336Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:5/block:2/seg:0",
      "source": "NVMe changes the calculus:",
      "source_hash": 16022564533278369819,
      "context_hash": 8344931007572651906,
      "translation": "NVMe는 이러한 셈법을 바꿉니다:",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "NVMe": "NVMe"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T21:50:07.921337Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:5/block:3/seg:0",
      "source": "No seek latency: request order is irrelevant to performance.",
      "source_hash": 772809909406623835,
      "context_hash": 13414210433750770172,
      "translation": "탐색(seek) 지연 시간이 없습니다: 요청 순서는 성능과 무관합니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "latency": "지연 시간"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T23:28:59.514998Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:5/block:4/seg:0",
      "source": "Hardware does its own internal scheduling across NAND dies.",
      "source_hash": 16727136632591129288,
      "context_hash": 17205267581027987301,
      "translation": "하드웨어가 NAND 다이 전반에 걸쳐 자체적으로 내부 스케줄링을 수행합니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "hardware": "하드웨어",
        "scheduling": "스케줄링"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T21:50:07.921337Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:5/block:5/seg:0",
      "source": "Adding a software scheduler introduces latency (requests wait in the scheduler queue) with zero benefit.",
      "source_hash": 6082883738564537808,
      "context_hash": 7508572836502688394,
      "translation": "소프트웨어 스케줄러를 추가하면 아무런 이점 없이 지연 시간만 늘어납니다(요청이 스케줄러 큐에서 대기합니다).",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "latency": "지연 시간",
        "queue": "큐",
        "scheduler": "스케줄러"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T23:28:59.514998Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:5/block:6/seg:0",
      "source": "NVMe devices therefore use the `none` scheduler by default.",
      "source_hash": 7255396343331594658,
      "context_hash": 7502679122032003601,
      "translation": "따라서 NVMe 디바이스는 기본적으로 `none` 스케줄러를 사용합니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "NVMe": "NVMe",
        "devices": "디바이스",
        "scheduler": "스케줄러"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T21:50:07.921337Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:5/block:6/seg:1",
      "source": "The scheduler infrastructure is still present in `request_queue` for SATA SSDs and HDDs, but it's bypassed entirely on NVMe paths.",
      "source_hash": 4334035866971343589,
      "context_hash": 8515364484086238353,
      "translation": "스케줄러 인프라는 SATA SSD와 HDD를 위해 여전히 `request_queue`에 존재하지만, NVMe 경로에서는 완전히 우회됩니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "HDDs": "HDD",
        "NVMe": "NVMe",
        "SSDs": "SSD",
        "scheduler": "스케줄러"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T21:50:07.921337Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:5/block:7/seg:0",
      "source": "The full story of how this led to the blk-mq redesign is in [blk-mq](blk-mq.md).",
      "source_hash": 14133306520650682733,
      "context_hash": 5412590263120186407,
      "translation": "이것이 어떻게 blk-mq 재설계로 이어졌는지에 대한 전체 이야기는 [blk-mq](blk-mq.md)에 있습니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "blk-mq": "blk-mq"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T21:50:07.921338Z",
      "issues": []
    },
